#
# Counter-example for the `math:` expression lowering
# (crates/logic/src/physical/lower.rs, MathLoweringError::CyclicExpressionGraph): TWO
# math:ApplicationExpression nodes whose single math:argumentSlot each names the
# OTHER as its math:slotExpression — a fully closed cycle through the
# math:slotExpression graph. Neither ex:cycleA nor ex:cycleB is a
# math:` expression "root" (`MathGraph::expression_roots`): each is referenced by the
# other's math:argumentSlot, so neither is an "unreferenced" candidate — the lowering's
# rootless-cyclic-component seeding path (`math_expression_structural_keys`) picks the
# lexicographically-first still-unvisited expression-typed node as an orphan root and
# walks into the cycle, and the cycle guard (`visiting`, a node reached while an
# ancestor of the SAME call is still being lowered) raises
# math:CyclicExpressionGraph on the second visit. The authored math:structuralKey on
# BOTH nodes lets the reasoned-graph gate (check_structural_key_on_rejected_expression)
# reach whichever one the deterministic orphan-seeding picks.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:cycleA a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:cycleSlotA ;
    math:structuralKey "not-a-real-digest" .

ex:cycleSlotA a math:ArgumentSlot ;
    math:slotIndex 0 ;
    math:slotExpression ex:cycleB .

ex:cycleB a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:cycleSlotB ;
    math:structuralKey "not-a-real-digest" .

ex:cycleSlotB a math:ArgumentSlot ;
    math:slotIndex 0 ;
    math:slotExpression ex:cycleA .
